{"type":"text","timestamp":1794343178016,"sessionID":"ses_e38daf826ffeth1zlvvxB2lzX3","part":{"id":"prt_1c7300f0a001uWIe2NzNXsDpJR","messageID":"msg_1c72ff50f0010NsyvLuqjLWS2b","sessionID":"ses_e38daf826ffeth1zlvvxB2lzX3","type":"text","text":"Done. The app is fully implemented and verified end-to-end.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): token-based auth (register/login), SQLite schema for users/tokens/customers/interactions, and all endpoints — health, auth, customers CRUD with paging/search/company filter, interaction log/create. Duplicate email returns 409 with a field error; omitted optional fields are cleared on PUT; `last_contacted_at`/`interaction_count` are computed via subqueries; deleting a customer cascades to its interactions.\n\n**Frontend** (React + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`): sign-in/registration screen, paged customer table with search + company filter, customer detail page with edit/delete and interaction log + log form, and add/edit forms showing API validation (including the duplicate-email message).\n\nVerified: unit-style API tests pass, `npm run build` succeeds, and gunicorn serves both `/api/health` and the SPA.\n\nNote: I added a `tsconfig.json` (the build script `tsc -b` required it, and it wasn't in the repo). New deps were added to `package.json`; `package-lock.json` was updated by `npm install`. The `.gitignore` doesn't exist yet — you may want to add one ignoring `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `__pycache__/`, `*.tsbuildinfo`, and `data/*.db` (the `.dockerignore` already handles image context).","time":{"start":1794343177994,"end":1794343177997}}}
